From b759373a0c574a63840e7d6b558d8dea61491b18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:45:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: 5P-8P labels over the players' racers, from a texture
 of our own

The game draws "1P".."4P" over human racers 0..3 and "COM" over CPUs from
36x30 rectangles of its HUD atlas ("Icon_Eff_E" in GTSE), picked by racer
index; a human racer 4..7 reads other sprites (character heads). The atlas
has no room for four more labels, so they come from a texture of our own:
the srnp_etiquettes file mod (built from the user's disc, outside any
repository) adds to GTSE a "SRNPLBL1" block, a palette and 256x32 C8 texels
(5P..8P), the file compressed again no bigger than the game's (from a save
state, the file table in RAM is the original disc's).

When the loaded GTSE carries that block, srnp_labels patches the two label
functions (1P HUD 0x8042F47C, split screen 0x804297C8): the rectangle comes
from a table of ours (the game's 1P-4P and COM, our 5P-8P) and the label's
quad goes through a 36-word routine that binds our texture around the
game's quad for 5P-8P. The routine sits in zero padding of the first code
section (0x80004D40): run from low memory, it hung the game. The label left
out (the player's own racer) stays the game's or the spotter's.

Measured (2 runners, 8 seats in lockstep, one with the labels, one without):
43 checksums equal, 0 divergences in JIT64; 38 equal, 0 divergences native;
29 equal with the HD pack at 1080p on one side.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
